import Gimle.Forseti.LocalTrapping
import Gimle.Forseti.Examples.GalerkinNS.T3

/-! # The 3-mode member below its laminar level: `E ≤ 12`

For `T3` (`ν = 1/10`, `f = 1`, start `(1, 1, 1)`) every set `Nonlinear.Trapping`
can trap contains the laminar point, where `E = 25/2`. This module traps a set
that does not: an ellipsoid `V = (x − c)ᵀ P (x − c) ≤ 1` with cross terms and a
centre near the equilibrium the start approaches in simulation (not a Lean
statement), found by gimle-forseti's spike 196
(`docs/spikes/196-cross-term-trapping/`), on which `V' ≤ α (inner − V)` holds
with `inner < 1` by an explicit sum of squares with an S-procedure multiplier
`σ ≥ 0`: `α (inner − V) − V' + σ (V − 1)` is a sum of squares everywhere, so on
the set, where `σ (V − 1) ≤ 0`, the decrease holds. The set lies in `{E ≤ 12}`
by an S-lemma certificate (`12 − E − τ (1 − V)` a sum of squares), so the
energy observation stays in `[0, 12]` for all time: below the laminar level,
below the family bound `13` of `trapping`.

All numbers are rational with denominator `10⁶` or derived exactly; every
identity is `ring`. The laminar point has `V ≈ 2.54 > 1`; the start has
`V = 0.98`. -/

namespace Gimle.Forseti.Examples.GalerkinNS.T3

open Gimle.Asgard Gimle.Asgard.Dynamics Gimle.Forseti Gimle.Forseti.Trajectory

